# Run S (2026-11-08, user: "lets start from c0 and freeze encoder", "also freeze GRU"):
# run Q's recipe (slurm/sac_scratch_2t_u5_orterm_idle_nb_a02.env: SAC, Town05 + Town01,
# one update every 5 env steps, off-road terminal with the junction rule, idle charge,
# arrival at any speed, temperature FIXED at 0.02, HER on) started FROM THE CLONE c0
# (il_bc_c0 step_15000: encoder, GRU and actor; fresh critics), with the encoder and
# GRU FROZEN for the whole run (IL_FREEZE_TRUNK=1) -- the actor head and the critic
# heads learn.
#
# Why (bottleneck, 2026-11-08): every from-scratch run drives 15-41 m per fault in the
# fixed-seed evals against c0's 262 m, and c0's encoder learned lane geometry from
# dense expert labels.
#
# Make-it-work settings for a warm start with an EMPTY replay, not experiment choices:
# LEARNING_STARTS=20000 (the trainer refuses less: the loaded policy refills the
# replay before any update) and IL_ONLINE_FREEZE_UPDATES=5000 (the actor waits 5000
# critic-only updates on c0's own driving, ~25k env steps at one update per 5, before
# it moves -- the warm-start rule). So steps 0-45k drive c0 itself: the 25k eval must
# reproduce c0 (68 of 80, no speed rule).
. "$REPO/slurm/sac_scratch_2t_u5_orterm_idle_nb_a02.env"
export INIT_FROM=$HOME/carla-rl/checkpoints/il_bc_c0/step_15000 LEARNING_STARTS=20000
export IL_FREEZE_TRUNK=1 IL_ONLINE_FREEZE_UPDATES=5000
